From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:10:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] alsa: a start on a suspended PCM is expected, not an error

A start that the driver refused is retried one period later from the
write path. A system sleep can suspend the PCM in between, which is what
happens when the kernel withdraws speaker protection for the sleep (its
start refusals began just before userspace froze). After the resume,
the retry then failed with -EBADFD and was logged as an error, and the
next avail check (-ESTRPIPE) had alsa_recover() resume or re-prepare the
stream as it should.

Report a start that fails because the PCM is SUSPENDED at info level,
through the same rate limit. Recovery is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 spa/plugins/alsa/alsa-pcm.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/spa/plugins/alsa/alsa-pcm.c b/spa/plugins/alsa/alsa-pcm.c
--- a/spa/plugins/alsa/alsa-pcm.c
+++ b/spa/plugins/alsa/alsa-pcm.c
@@ -2786,6 +2786,7 @@
 static inline int do_start(struct state *state)
 {
 	int res, suppressed;
+	bool suspended;
 	if (SPA_UNLIKELY(!state->alsa_started)) {
 		spa_log_debug(state->log, "%p: snd_pcm_start linked:%u", state, state->linked);
 		if (!state->linked && (res = snd_pcm_start(state->hndl)) < 0) {
@@ -2800,10 +2801,19 @@
 				(uint64_t)state->threshold * SPA_NSEC_PER_SEC / state->rate :
 				SPA_NSEC_PER_MSEC * 10;
 			state->start_retry_time = now + period;
+			/* A system sleep can suspend the PCM between a refused start
+			 * and its retry. The start then fails with -EBADFD, and the
+			 * next avail check (-ESTRPIPE) has alsa_recover() resume or
+			 * re-prepare the stream: expected, not an error. */
+			suspended = (res == -EBADFD || res == -ESTRPIPE) &&
+				snd_pcm_state(state->hndl) == SND_PCM_STATE_SUSPENDED;
 			if ((suppressed = spa_ratelimit_test(&state->start_limit, now)) >= 0) {
 				if (res == -EPERM)
 					spa_log_info(state->log, "%s: snd_pcm_start: %s, retrying (%d suppressed)",
 							state->name, snd_strerror(res), suppressed);
+				else if (suspended)
+					spa_log_info(state->log, "%s: snd_pcm_start: stream suspended by a system sleep, "
+							"recovering (%d suppressed)", state->name, suppressed);
 				else
 					spa_log_error(state->log, "%s: snd_pcm_start: %s (%d suppressed)",
 							state->name, snd_strerror(res), suppressed);
